<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Proclamation of 1763</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1763</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Royal Proclamation of 1763 was issued by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s North American territories in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1763">Treaty of Paris</a>. It created the provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a>, East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> and West Florida and reserved the lands west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appalachian-mountains">Appalachians</a> for Indigenous nations, forbidding settlement there. The restriction angered colonists, and the proclamation remains a basis of Indigenous rights in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/royal-proclamation-of-1763.jpg" alt="Royal Proclamation of 1763" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: King George III · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Proclamation_of_1763.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
